course: dictionary
lesson: 5616
title: Lightness: heavy, pale or cheerful?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word lightness has three main meanings. The first is not being heavy, like the lightness of a feather. The second is being bright or pale in colour. The third is a gentle, cheerful feeling, like lightness of heart.
explain: Use the words around the word to choose the right meaning. «Many people feel real relief and lightness after an honest confession.» Relief means a worry has gone, so lightness here is the happy, easy feeling that comes when a weight lifts off your mind.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Heaviness does not fit here, because heaviness is the opposite of lightness, so the right meaning must be the cheerful feeling. If your meaning still makes sense, you have probably got it right.
fact: Lightness is a noun, so it names a quality that you can talk about.
fact: «Lightness» can mean not heavy, as in the lightness of a feather.
fact: «Lightness» can mean bright or pale in colour, as in the lightness of a painted wall.
fact: «Lightness» can mean a gentle, cheerful feeling, as in lightness of heart or lightness of step.
fact: Lightness is uncountable, so we say «much lightness», not «many lightnesses».
exercise: «Many people feel real relief and lightness after an honest confession.» What does lightness mean here? | *A gentle, cheerful feeling | Wet and slippery ground | Pale grey paint on a wall | A heavy, sad weight in the chest
exercise: Which one shows lightness meaning not heavy? | *A feather floating gently down | A thick stone wall | A dark, stormy sea | A heavy iron anchor
exercise: Lightness can mean bright or pale in colour. Which is an example? | *A soft, pale yellow wall | A black, heavy coat | Loud music from the street | Slow, tired walking
test: The dancer's lightness made her look as if she was floating across the stage. What does lightness suggest here? | Being angry with the crowd | Being tired and slow | *Being graceful and light on her feet | Being cold
test: Which phrase uses lightness to mean a cheerful feeling? | Heaviness of heart | Darkness of the night | *Lightness of heart | Weight of the rock
exam: Ella says, «Her lightness after the test showed she felt free.» What does lightness mean here? | Being dark in colour | *A cheerful, easy feeling | Being slow | Being heavy
